From: "VItoriaBr CEO (local)" <ceo-local@localhost>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 15:01:38 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 8/9] NVIDIA faces: 16-bit values read through integer views
 (port of 77e13a9, faces part)

Port of trustno1-coder's 77e13a9 (faces part only) and of fxceless pull
request 927: the face network's 16-bit values travel through integer
views. A translated program that moves halves reads them as floats; on
NVIDIA they came back zero, so faces went black or missing.

Taken: emit/halves.rs (new), lower.rs (half-view lowering; also carries
the VICTORY_NAN_SCRUB switch of 77e13a9, off unless set),
descriptor/host.rs (conflict resolved in favour of the upstream text),
draw.rs (table binds with half views), shader_cache.rs (half_views kept
in the cache), and the shader tests that build HostShader.

NOT taken: the colour-target part of the same commit
(VICTORY_TARGET_VARIANTS, a35c557: TargetFormats, host_pipeline_for,
bound_format). Its merge onto this branch conflicts in draw.rs,
pipeline/host.rs and pipeline/make.rs. So a draw into a render target of
another format than its pipeline declares keeps the old lookup.

Not taken either: README, scripts/play-nvidia.ps1, rt_off_hashes.txt,
ambient, capture, pipeline wait, texture video fix.

Cherry-pick was not usable (-x would bring the whole commit); this is a
hand port citing 77e13a9 as the origin.

Disable: this change has no switch; revert this commit.
